# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. Real values live in Vercel's
# environment variables and never in the repository.

# The origin canonical URLs and Open Graph tags are built from. Leave this
# unset on Vercel: each preview then points at itself and production points at
# rabaedapp.com.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# The launch switch. Until this is `true` on Vercel's *production*
# environment, every page tells search engines and AI crawlers not to index it.
# Ticket 39 sets it as the deliberate go-live step; nothing else should.
# SITE_INDEXABLE=true

# --- The CMS (ticket 19). See "The CMS" in docs/deployment.md. ---------------
#
# Locally, leave all of these unset: `npm run dev` starts a database of its own
# in `.data/postgres` and keeps uploaded images in `.data/media`.

# The Supabase Postgres connection string (Project Settings → Database).
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://...

# Signs editors' login sessions. A long random value, different per environment.
# PAYLOAD_SECRET=

# Supabase Storage, through its S3 interface (Project Settings → Storage).
# All five or none; a Vercel deployment refuses to start with none.
# S3_BUCKET=media
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/storage/v1/s3
# S3_REGION=
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- Email (ticket 27). See "Email" in docs/deployment.md. --------------------
#
# The Microsoft 365 no-reply mailbox the forms send from. Both or neither.
# Without them the site works the same and sends no email; each submission
# records that its mail was not sent.
# MAIL_USER=no-reply@rabaedapp.com
# MAIL_PASSWORD=
